.\" QtDMM manual page. CMake fills in version and date (docs/qtdmm.1.in).
.\" The options must match src/main.cpp - tests/generate_docs.py --check
.\" (ctest docs_generated) compares them.
.TH QTDMM 1 "@QTDMM_MAN_DATE@" "QtDMM @QTDMM_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qtdmm \- read out and record digital multimeters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qtdmm
.RB [ \-\-config\-id
.IR id ]
.RB [ \-\-config\-dir
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-\-debug ]
.br
.B qtdmm
.BR \-h " | " \-\-help " | " \-v " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B QtDMM
reads digital multimeters and bench meters and shows the reading as an LCD
display and an analog meter. A configurable recorder draws the readings as a
graph. It can start by hand, at a set time or when a threshold is crossed, and
exports to CSV, Excel (.xlsx), OpenDocument (.ods), SVG, PDF, PNG and JPEG.
.PP
More than 150 meters are supported, connected over:
.IP \(bu 2
serial ports and USB\-serial cables;
.IP \(bu 2
USB\-HID cables such as the UNI\-T UT\-D04/UT\-D09 and Brymen BU\-86X;
.IP \(bu 2
the network (RFC 2217, for example through
.BR qtdmm\-bridge );
.IP \(bu 2
Bluetooth LE (UNI\-T UT60BT, Victron battery monitors, solar chargers and
inverters);
.IP \(bu 2
.BR sigrok\-cli (1)
for SCPI bench meters.
.PP
Further features are a readings table, alarms with actions, calculated values
across several meters, a virtual meter for trying QtDMM without hardware, and
an SCPI server through which other programs read the meter over the network.
The complete handbook is built into the program (Help) and online at
.UR https://qtdmm.de/docs/
.UE .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-id " id"
Use the configuration
.I id
instead of
.BR default .
Each id has its own settings file, so one meter can be set up per id; several
instances with different ids run side by side and know about each other.
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-dir " dir"
Keep the configuration files in
.I dir
instead of the platform's user configuration directory.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Print every frame received from the meter as a line of hex bytes on
standard output.
Include this output, together with what the meter displayed, in a bug report
about a meter that is not decoded correctly.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/QtDMM/QtDMM.conf
Settings of the
.B default
configuration (Linux, FreeBSD and macOS).
.TP
.IR ~/.config/QtDMM/QtDMM_ id .conf
Settings of the configuration
.IR id .
.TP
.I %APPDATA%\eQtDMM\eQtDMM.ini
Settings on Windows; further ids as
.IR QtDMM_ id .ini .
.SH EXAMPLES
Start a second instance for another meter:
.PP
.RS
.B qtdmm \-\-config\-id power\-supply
.RE
.PP
Capture the raw frames of a meter for a bug report:
.PP
.RS
.B qtdmm \-\-debug > frames.txt
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sigrok\-cli (1)
.PP
Handbook:
.UR https://qtdmm.de/docs/
.UE
.br
Source and bug reports:
.UR https://github.com/qtdmm/QtDMM
.UE
.br
Contact: hello@qtdmm.de
